{"type":"text","timestamp":1795090891985,"sessionID":"ses_e0c3ed877ffeAphuqZVFIJlauE","part":{"id":"prt_1f3c141ef001jnlIHpc0saXo1H","messageID":"msg_1f3c12b76001VKkXn90vbkb0h3","sessionID":"ses_e0c3ed877ffeAphuqZVFIJlauE","type":"text","text":"The Pythagorean theorem applies to right triangles: the square of the hypotenuse (the side opposite the right angle) equals the sum of the squares of the other two sides.\n\n**a² + b² = c²**, where *c* is the hypotenuse and *a*, *b* are the legs.\n\nExample: if the legs are 3 and 4, then c² = 9 + 16 = 25, so c = 5.","time":{"start":1795090891247,"end":1795090891977}}}
